.el .ds Aq '
.TH pgloupe-logs-dump 1  "dump " 
.SH NAME
pgloupe\-logs\-dump \- Decode a log (csvlog, jsonlog or stderr; compression is detected) and print each record as JSON
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpgloupe logs dump\fR [\fB\-\-format\fR] [\fB\-\-prefix\fR] [\fB\-\-log\-tz\fR] [\fB\-\-limit\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIFILE\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Decode a log (csvlog, jsonlog or stderr; compression is detected) and print each record as JSON
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-format\fR \fI<FORMAT>\fR [default: auto]
Log format; `auto` looks at the first line
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
auto
.IP \(bu 2
csv
.IP \(bu 2
json
.IP \(bu 2
stderr
.IP \(bu 2
pgbouncer: The pgBouncer log (experimental)
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-prefix\fR \fI<PREFIX>\fR
The server\*(Aqs `log_line_prefix`; required for stderr logs
.TP
\fB\-\-log\-tz\fR \fI<LOG_TZ>\fR
Offset for timezone abbreviations the log does not spell out, e.g. `\-03` or `+05:30`
.TP
\fB\-\-limit\fR \fI<LIMIT>\fR
Stop after this many records
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
<\fIFILE\fR>
Log file; compression is detected automatically
